WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>To all staff members of Chaldea...</i>

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>Today's working hours
will end at 17:00.</i>

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.740
<i>You could consider it a nice touch
from the deputy commander.</i>

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.160
<i>You won't be able
to quite call it Christmas break,</i>

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.740
<i>but please make sure
that you all get enough rest.</i>

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.120
<i>Also, concerning the Inquiry Board
whose arrival has been delayed,</i>

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.920
<i>it has been set that they will arrive
as soon as the weather improves.</i>

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.630
<i>They are scheduled
to arrive at 12:00 tomorrow.</i>

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.640
<i>We expect you to act with moderation and pride
as current staff members of Chaldea.</i>

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.220
<i>Our work will be passed
onto the new staff at the end of 2017,</i>

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>but until then, please continue
your work with responsibility...</i>

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.770
I guess the inquiry's starting now.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.480
What are you guys going to do?

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.230
You guys were sent here
from the Clock Tower, right?

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.030
We're going back to London.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.490
We don't like how things are, but we can't
stay in our current situation forever.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.830
After all, this organization
belongs to the United Nations.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.160
I wish I could stay here.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.210
They have great equipment here,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.960
and I've grown attached to this place
after protecting it for a year.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.250
In the first place,

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.380
I don't think the new staff would be able
to properly keep Chaldea running!

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.090
Thank you for your hard work!

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.350
Duston, um, do you have a moment?

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.850
Of course. Is something
the matter, Kyrielight?

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.560
I'm looking for Senpai...

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.730
I meant, Cadet Ritsuka Fujimaru... I have
a message for him, but I can't find him.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.190
It seems that comm
has been disconnected.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.480
Fujimaru?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.490
Come to think of it,
I didn't see him at the cafeteria.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.610
He wasn't in the medical office
or the simulator, either...

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.370
when I was doing the lockdown.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.540
Then, what I saw earlier...
It wasn't just me.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.540
You know the warehouse area
behind the command room, right?

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.260
The one that used to be a break room
or a salon, and got renovated.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.090
I saw someone
who looked like Ritsuka from behind.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.100
Thank you for the information.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.470
But, um,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.850
is there a problem
with the back warehouse?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.730
No, it's just that most staff
don't go near that place.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.190
It's because the Lostroom is located there.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.690
Lostroom?

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.200
Yeah, it's somewhat of a ghost story.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.410
There were many reports about people
entering the place at midnight

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.120
and seeing things that were lost
or soon will be lost.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.290
It's a Relic from the days
of the previous director,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.750
now long lost as a warehouse.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.320
I won't allow for a restoration of humanity
controlled by the caste system!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.280
Such a society where a person's fate
is determined as they're born...

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.660
I'll never let it happen!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.450
Go forth, Berserker!

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.850
You did it, Director!

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:30.890
This is only natural!

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.650
Who do you think I am?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.480
I am the director of Chaldea,
and the current head of Astromancy,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.400
Olga Marie Animusphere!

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.570
You can see what I can do
if I'm suitable to be a Master!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.450
You're not the only one
who can look high and mighty!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.000
Look out!

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.210
Behind you!

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.270
I have no business with Heroic Spirits
from the Age of Gods.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.190
This planet belongs to humans now.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.870
A ruler who claims to be a deity
is way too out-of-date!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.320
Archer! Caster!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.390
Jeez. You guys cannot win without me.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.400
<i>Mash? Fujimaru?</i>

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.520
<i>Where did you go?</i>

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.650
<i>Wasn't I doing a good job
as a Master just now?</i>

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.530
<i>Hey! What's the meaning of all this?</i>

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.530
<i>Have I been asleep?</i>

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.490
<i>I feel like I was having a strange dream.</i>

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.250
Olga, can I continue the conversation?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.620
Lev?

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.250
S-Sure.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.880
Go ahead. What were you talking about?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:06.260
It was about the unknown point observed
by Chaldeas the other day, Director.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.010
Oh, that's right.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.350
This is a serious situation we have here.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.310
It may end up becoming a Singularity
that disrupts human history

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.350
that has been solidified to the present.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.150
How am I going to report this
to the Association and to the UN?

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.320
I think it's too early to make a report.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.650
This may have been
a malfunction of Chaldeas.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.530
It's already been 11 years
since it was officially activated in 2004.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.490
How about we give it
a good maintenance for once?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.080
We can't do that.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:41.210
Chaldeas is a pseudo-heavenly body
that copied and re-outputted the soul of Earth.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:45.550
Now that we got it running,
stopping it is as good as killing it.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.340
Besides, my Chaldeas wouldn't have
any imperfections.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:53.800
If there's an issue at all,
it has to be from some external factor.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.930
External factor...

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.520
If Chaldeas has no issues,

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:03.060
does that mean the malfunction
is with Sheba, the lens that observes it?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.440
Oh, does that mean it's my fault?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.820
Indeed, my Sheba has been running
for ten years, as well.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.450
Perhaps, the logic within it
has gotten antiquated here and there.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.700
I didn't blame you, Lev!

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.420
Fatigue of staff members in the control room
or harassment from the Association...

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.830
Possibilities of that nature exist, as well!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.050
The health of the staff
has been well-maintained.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.260
But I personally would like you to rest
as much as the others do, Director.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.260
Agreed.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.760
Ever since Chaldeas showed
abnormalities a week ago,

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.520
you haven't been sleeping much,
have you Olga?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.350
You should have the doctor
take a look at you.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.690
The Rayshift experiment report...

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.820
and the accompanying request for selecting
the Master candidates have been approved.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.860
Director, you need to have
your mandatory rest of 12 hours.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.660
Please take care of yourself.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.410
We no longer have anyone to take your place.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.670
Right. I'll take that as word of advice.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.290
Speaking of, Professor Lev,
you've been getting a good amount of sleep.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.300
I hear that you're an early riser
and early sleeper, and thus very healthy.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.550
Yes. I was a workaholic
before coming to Chaldea, though.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.310
But since Sheba has been completed,
I haven't had any dreams.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.520
Thanks to that, I've been
a sound sleeper at night.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.650
Romani, how about you?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.400
I'm the opposite.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.280
I keep having dreams
ever since I came here.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.690
It's always the same one,

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.740
though it's really not much of a dream.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.490
<i>Chaldea Security Organization...</i>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.540
<i>An organization built by my father
to secure our future.</i>

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.920
<i>Since ancient times,
my family, the Animuspheres,</i>

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.670
<i>has been a Mage family that studies
and controls movements of heavenly bodies.</i>

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.890
<i>The mission of an Animusphere...</i>

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.760
<i>and the duties that the entire family
must make sure to fulfill...</i>

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.600
<i>The Grand Order.</i>

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:06.190
<i>That is none other than the security
of this planet and of human history.</i>

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.230
<i>My family has watched over human history,</i>

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:13.990
<i>and saw to it that beyond it,
the future continues with certainty.</i>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.070
<i>We don't talk big, like asserting
that we create the future.</i>

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:22.660
<i>However, our mission was to relay
to the other Mages that a future exists,</i>

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.790
<i>and to guarantee that it is so.</i>

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.750
<i>The Animuspheres, as a result,
created this Mystic Code.</i>

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.300
<i>Chaldeas, a pseudo-heavenly body.</i>

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.430
<i>Hypothesizing that a planet has a soul,</i>

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:41.260
<i>we copied that soul and outputted it
as a microscopic model case.</i>

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.730
<i>We can't meddle
with this other Earth at all,</i>

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.850
<i>as it is in a different phase.</i>

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.150
<i>But we can still observe it like this.</i>

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.240
<i>My father set Chaldeas to be
100 years in the future.</i>

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:59.740
<i>If Chaldeas is lit
with the lights of civilization,</i>

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:03.200
<i>we can prove that humanity still exists
100 years in the future.</i>

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.960
<i>Simultaneously, Chaldeas has functioned
as a library for Earth.</i>

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:12.130
<i>One cannot observe the details
of 100 years in the future...</i>

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.800
<i>because the future is variable.</i>

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.090
<i>But you can draw out the details of the past
that have already been determined.</i>

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.140
<i>In other words, it's a compass for when you head
toward the past events of human history.</i>

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:28.560
<i>Rayshifting, which disintegrates the human body
into Spiritrons and outputs them into the past,</i>

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.820
<i>will show a dramatic increase
in its success rate with Chaldeas to assist.</i>

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.070
<i>My father built Chaldeas and operated it,</i>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:41.910
<i>creating Chaldea
as an organization to observe it.</i>

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.950
<i>He was a noble researcher
and a great Mage.</i>

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.750
<i>And he passed away from this realm
three years ago, leaving me behind.</i>

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:55.250
<i>His body was found
in the director's room in 2012.</i>

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:01.260
<i>It's still unknown whether he died
from illness or an accident.</i>

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:06.520
<i>I'm just a naïve girl who took over Chaldea
after my father's death.</i>

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.560
<i>My father didn't leave me
anything behind,</i>

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.520
<i>but I was handed down
the beliefs as a Mage of Animusphere.</i>

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.280
<i>It's been almost two years
since I took over as the director.</i>

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.530
<i>Even though I was a girl
who didn't know so much,</i>

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.280
<i>I thought I'd finally
gotten used to this, but still...</i>

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.540
But why is it 100 years in the future?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.920
What do you mean by that, Mash?

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:32.250
Well...

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:36.590
if you just want to observe
that there's still a civilization tomorrow,

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.470
I think it can be simply one day
or one year in the future.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.300
Because we need enough time
to respond, Mash.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.930
If the light of civilization
for tomorrow has been extinguished,

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.890
you have a dire situation
you can no longer do anything about.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.520
However, if the ruin comes
a year or ten years down the line,

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.360
you get all that much more time
to set up countermeasures.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.990
The reason why the previous director
set it up for 100 years in the future...

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.700
is to give enough time
for countermeasures to humanity, I think.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:09.160
I see. So, the previous director
had thought about it that far.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.210
O-Of course!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:15.210
My father was a thoughtful
and a very careful person.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:19.550
He wasn't the type to move things along
simply from conjectures or wishful thinking.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.630
I'm sure.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:26.970
He probably also kept the Heroic Spirit summoning
system going to prepare for situations like this.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.060
If some abnormality
were to occur in the past,

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.690
we in present time can't extract
the lesion in the past.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:38.900
If so, we must head directly to that time in the past
and resolve the situation on the spot.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.610
Even if the Rayshift is a success,

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.360
the only things we can take with us
are the physical bodies of the Mages.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.950
They have no weapons
to rely on once there.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.490
That's why Heroic Spirits...

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.910
Servants are necessary.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.160
No matter how mutated it is,

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.960
as long as it's an extension
of human history, Heroic Spirits will exist.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.800
And if you can get their help,

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.470
you can fight
no matter what era you are in.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.430
I see.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.140
Heroic Spirits
are high-tier astral phenomena.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:12.310
The Throne of Heroes is in a dimension
higher than the one we are in after all.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.190
They transcend time itself.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.860
There can be no companion
better suited for the methodology...

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.980
of securing humanity that Chaldea uses.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.700
Because they'll appear in any era
once you make a contract with them.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:29.620
That Heroic Spirit summoning system
is not stable yet.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:35.620
Securing Master candidates
who are suitable for Rayshifts is important,

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.250
but we must somehow further
test things on that end, as well.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.010
It would be nice if Da Vinci
was a bit more cooperative with us.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:48.640
Olga, how about you give him,
I mean her, a Workshop to use?

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.260
It's too early for that!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.520
I can't trust any Servants
who have no Masters.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.520
Besides, I don't get along
with that Heroic Spirit to begin with.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:01.020
When we have our next successful summons,
I'll have her depart right away!

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.780
That sounds pretty harsh.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:07.780
Da Vinci might say she thinks
of the director like a little sister.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.160
Just leave the Heroic Spirit
summons to Da Vinci.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.660
We need to select the Masters.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.290
Was the selection of the A-team final, Olga?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.330
Yes.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:24.630
Besides, my father left an instruction to choose
those seven in case of an emergency.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:29.890
Though, my father called them "Crypters"
instead of "Master candidates."

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.140
Director...

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:33.720
What is this?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.480
It doesn't look like something
created in Chaldea.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.140
Oh, that is...

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.730
Wait, it's strange.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.570
It is supposed to be securely stored.

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.820
Oh, I'm sorry.
Was it something very valuable?

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.200
It's fine! It won't be used anymore.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.830
That is one of the gifts
from the Atlas Academy.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.740
Atlas Academy?

00:14:55.240 --> 00:15:00.080
The same Atlas Academy as the one
that provided the blueprints for Trismegistus,

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.830
the heart of Chaldea?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.290
Right.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.840
The weapons armory
of the Magecraft world.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:07.840
The cellar of taboos.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.550
The Atlas Academy...

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.800
My father had a contract from Atlas.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:18.180
He asked them for their technology
in exchange for the contract.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:22.480
One of them was the Spiritron
Calculation Engine, Trismegistus.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.900
And the other one is that thing.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.780
Void-Reality Observation Device,
Paper Moon.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.070
Paper Moon...

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.530
A two-dimensional moon, huh?

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.120
That's something I haven't heard before.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.370
So, how do you actually use it?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.330
It's a compass for observing
and substantiating Void Space.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:48.260
I heard it was prepared in order to overcome
the phase differential with Chaldeas.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.630
That said, it's useless now anyway.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:56.010
Now that Sheba has been completed,
we can perform Rayshift.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.970
This is a surprise.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:02.310
Was there another way to access
Singularities besides Rayshifts?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:08.030
Yes. It was a way to transport by diving into
Void Space, then floating up into the destination.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.190
It was called "Zero Sail."

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:13.280
And we named the ship
that made it all possible...

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.580
"Shadow Border."
That's what we secretly named it.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.040
So I see.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:27.380
There was a machine that was no longer
put to use because I had completed Sheba.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.670
That was something I overlooked.

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.680
No wonder why I was insulted
as being blind.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.680
Lev?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.260
Oh, I'm just being sentimental.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:42.180
There's something I'd like to confess.
Well, this is the last time anyway...

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.190
I'll just chalk this up
to being delusional.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:47.110
Olga,

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:56.530
I completed the Near-Future Observation Lens:
Sheba, in 1999 by Marisbury's request.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:17:00.200
At that point, my destiny
had been set in stone.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.660
Saving humanity...

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.580
No, that's not it.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.290
Making this planet better...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:09.840
That was the goal of my life.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:13.470
Before this happened
and after this happened.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:19.350
The future that humanity builds
is multi-colored, full of changes,

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.560
and that's why it's so unstable.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:25.850
Even if humanity had
a wonderful and giant load,

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.730
if they trip on a pebble,
it all goes back to square one, right?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.610
I had been hoping
to get rid of such risk.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.360
There's not much I can do.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:39.870
However, I thought I could
at least move the pebble.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.240
What about you?

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.880
Do you want to become that load,
or the person carrying it,

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:51.630
or something
that moves the pebbles away?

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.880
I... am...

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.930
<i>I am none of those.</i>

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:05.060
<i>I only doubt if I can be responsible
for securing humanity.</i>

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.400
<i>I don't care about the future
or how valuable it is.</i>

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:15.900
<i>I only have an obsessive idea
about having to prove I'm competent.</i>

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.410
<i>Every day is hard on me.</i>

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:20.910
<i>There is no future in everyday life.</i>

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:24.330
<i>What do I need to do to end this?</i>

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.960
<i>What do I need to have
in order to be happy?</i>

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.920
<i>Unless I know the answers
to those questions,</i>

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.670
<i>how can I know my objectives?</i>

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:45.100
It's this late already?

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.980
I have to excuse myself.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:52.360
I'm going to be very busy from now on.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.490
<i>So, you're Olga Marie?</i>

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.620
<i>I'm Lev Lainur. Nice to meet you.</i>

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.830
<i>Oh, no handshakes?</i>

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.250
<i>That's fine. It's worth working for.</i>

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.380
<i>Trust is something
that takes time to gain.</i>

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:22.550
<i>You say my outfit is strange?
I stand out?</i>

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:26.020
<i>Of course I do.
I'm the only anachronistic one here.</i>

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:30.440
<i>But this is my pride as a Mage,</i>

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.900
<i>and my way of respecting
the history of your Animusphere Family.</i>

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:39.610
<i>Even though this is a modern facility,
it's still an Animusphere Workshop.</i>

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:44.370
<i>If so, you should have at least one man
like me, a traditional, typical Mage.</i>

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.290
<i>Yes.</i>

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.170
<i>Farewell, Lev Lainur.</i>

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.140
Good morning!
Are you on break, as well, Senpai?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.190
Oh, so all of you are here.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.900
I'll get you something to drink.
What would you like?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.820
Then, I'll have some tea.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.200
I'll sit here if you don't mind.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.850
It's not like I'm worried
about you or anything,

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.020
but you look surprisingly glum.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.020
What are you so worried about?

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.740
There's just so many things I can't do well.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:05.570
Well, of course!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.740
You were brought here as a reserve
to make up the numbers after all.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:12.580
You're not a Mage nor a soldier!
Just an ordinary citizen.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.170
Normally, you don't get an opportunity
to be useful until the very end,

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.500
and you're never given
a chance for combat.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.590
I don't think you can play the great role
of protecting humanity's future—

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:22.630
Even so...

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.010
I thought I couldn't have everyone else
help me out all the time.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.020
And at least, I had to do something
I was capable of doing.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.770
So, I've been trying my best, but...

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.020
What are you...

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.610
The more time passes,

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.730
the more I realize that I'm mediocre.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.320
No matter how much I train,

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.070
no matter how much I study Magecraft...

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:49.830
Sometimes, when I'm alone like this, I think,

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.660
"Why me?"

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.750
"Surely, there was someone else
suited for this."

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.170
I start having negative thoughts like that.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.250
Are you saying that you becoming
a Master was a mistake?

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:05.420
That there were no other personnel,
so you're reluctantly doing this?

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:12.850
<i>Yes.</i>

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:16.940
<i>Why don't I just crush him right here?</i>

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:20.860
But well...

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.150
No matter how much I struggle,

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:26.650
it's true that I can't do anything.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.490
And if I can't escape from that fact,

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:31.830
I have to bluff and act tough at least.

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:36.460
If I am mediocre,

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:40.290
I have to demonstrate just how average
I am, or I'd really be useless.

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:44.000
I want to answer to everyone's trust
in me as Ritsuka Fujimaru,

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.880
not as someone else's substitute.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:50.140
I'm so disappointed in you!

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:54.520
To think the future of humanity
relies on someone who whines like that!

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:01.900
Restoring humanity is too big a burden
for your shoulders!

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:05.030
I must say that it was a mistake
in my own judgment.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:09.280
But we were able to come this far
thanks to you, Director.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:15.740
We were able to complete
the Order at Fuyuki thanks to you.

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:19.670
We were able to erase Singularities
in France, Rome and Okeanos...

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.000
thanks to your navigation.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:25.380
Me? I worked with you?

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:30.760
Mash, what year is it right now?

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.510
It's May 1, 2016 today.

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:45.730
Director? Are you not feeling well again?

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:47.780
It's nothing.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:49.860
Thank you, Mash.

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:54.370
I wish we could've chatted
like this a lot sooner.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.750
Fujimaru...

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:02.250
You're that scared,
yet you're not giving up?

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:07.250
Well, you know, I'll only give up
if I get discouraged a bit more.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:09.260
I see.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:16.140
I can't do anything for you any more,
but do know I'm cheering for you.

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:18.970
Even if your futures have been altered...

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:23.100
into something completely futile.

00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:28.480
By the way,

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:30.690
who was that?

00:24:30.690 --> 00:24:34.870
<i>That was nobody. She was someone
who couldn't reach this future.</i>

00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:54.760
Give up.

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:57.260
You guys cannot protect humanity.

00:25:53.940 --> 00:25:54.990
You, a wanderer from a distant future...

00:25:55.990 --> 00:25:59.870
Or rather,
from the correct version of history...

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:01.950
You have no chance of victory.

00:26:02.370 --> 00:26:04.500
The human world will perish.

00:26:05.250 --> 00:26:07.750
That's how the future has been fixed.

00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:12.380
I know someone
who said something like that.

00:26:13.550 --> 00:26:17.050
But it was only a castle in the clouds!

00:26:17.380 --> 00:26:20.850
As long as humans
with the will to fight remain,

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:23.350
the future is always a white canvas!

00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:25.890
There's no way it's already perished!

00:26:29.980 --> 00:26:31.360
Exactly.

00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:36.030
The future literally has become
a white canvas like you said.

00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:39.530
It is good if there's something
that will burn.

00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:43.290
And it's even better
if there's something left.

00:26:43.540 --> 00:26:47.330
But this planet
has let go of even those remnants.

00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:51.040
Humanity is at a dead end.

00:26:51.290 --> 00:26:53.210
This is one year in the future.

00:26:53.500 --> 00:26:57.680
This is what Earth will look like
in the future...

00:26:57.930 --> 00:27:00.180
after you demolish
the Incineration of Humanity.

00:27:00.970 --> 00:27:03.470
Once, the King of Mages said,

00:27:04.180 --> 00:27:07.430
"Your happiness lies in doing nothing."

00:27:08.310 --> 00:27:10.810
I'll repeat those words once more.

00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:15.280
Our history will not continue
into the future.

00:27:16.860 --> 00:27:18.110
Because...

00:27:18.990 --> 00:27:21.490
we restored humanity.

00:27:43.510 --> 00:27:45.560
Wake up, Fujimaru.

00:27:48.480 --> 00:27:51.150
I'm sorry, I had fallen asleep.

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:53.310
Huh?

00:27:55.070 --> 00:27:58.940
I just came here to drop some stuff off,
but I fell asleep...

00:27:59.490 --> 00:28:02.070
while everyone else in Chaldea
is busy cleaning up.

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:18.670
Senpai!

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:24.300
I was worried because I couldn't find you
in your room or the cafeteria!

00:28:24.550 --> 00:28:26.560
Were you in the warehouse?

00:28:26.810 --> 00:28:27.600
Yeah.

00:28:27.850 --> 00:28:32.310
I bundled up the sheets and tableware
I'd been using. I didn't want to throw them away.

00:28:33.100 --> 00:28:36.320
New staff from the Association
is arriving soon, right?

00:28:36.570 --> 00:28:40.240
Yes. As soon as the weather improves,
they'll come by helicopter.

00:28:40.570 --> 00:28:42.820
The boat is already docked
on the shoreline.

00:28:42.820 --> 00:28:43.820
I see.

00:28:44.820 --> 00:28:48.330
So much has happened in the past year,

00:28:49.080 --> 00:28:50.330
but it was fun.

00:28:54.880 --> 00:28:56.460
Thank you, Mash,

00:28:56.710 --> 00:29:00.210
for continually supporting
a mediocre Master like me.

00:29:01.340 --> 00:29:02.470
Oh no.

00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:04.970
I'm the one who should be
giving my thanks!

00:29:04.970 --> 00:29:09.970
I'm sure I've been supported by you
way more than I've supported you!

00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:20.570
The Inquiry Board's intent is clear.

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:24.740
The old Chaldea will be dismantled,
and the entire staff will be replaced.

00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:27.950
I'm not sure if I'll be able to stay
in the same department as you.

00:29:29.080 --> 00:29:32.750
Will you be able to remain
at Chaldea to begin with?

00:29:32.750 --> 00:29:36.920
If you're returning to your home in Japan,
would you give me your address?

00:29:36.920 --> 00:29:40.590
So that I can send you new year greetings!

00:29:46.180 --> 00:29:49.390
<i>The Board will arrive soon.</i>

00:29:50.100 --> 00:29:54.850
<i>Those miracle days I spent here in Chaldea
will end as they arrive.</i>

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:59.360
<i>I don't know what will happen
from now on.</i>

00:29:59.770 --> 00:30:01.480
<i>Even if I'm no longer a Master,</i>

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:04.990
<i>I'd be delighted if I could be employed
as a staff member of Chaldea.</i>

00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:07.620
<i>But I don't think things will go that well.</i>

00:30:08.870 --> 00:30:10.530
<i>But no matter what happens,</i>

00:30:10.780 --> 00:30:13.200
<i>no matter how much
I worry about the future,</i>

00:30:13.620 --> 00:30:15.540
<i>I don't think I'll ever be afraid.</i>

00:30:16.670 --> 00:30:18.790
<i>Basically, humans are powerless,</i>

00:30:18.790 --> 00:30:21.340
<i>and it's rare for things to go well.</i>

00:30:21.750 --> 00:30:23.760
<i>Usually, there's nothing to gain,</i>

00:30:23.760 --> 00:30:25.800
<i>and it's a part of everyday life
that you laugh it off,</i>

00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:28.010
<i>saying things happen.</i>

00:30:28.970 --> 00:30:33.140
<i>I realized that side of human nature
and its strength.</i>

00:30:33.560 --> 00:30:35.980
<i>And I was saved by it
in my short yet long journey.</i>

00:30:36.440 --> 00:30:37.560
<i>For now,</i>

00:30:38.060 --> 00:30:40.360
<i>there are still things that I can do!</i>

00:30:40.980 --> 00:30:43.070
<i>Holding that belief in my heart,</i>

00:30:43.400 --> 00:30:45.820
<i>I will start the new year.</i>
